{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169939-setting-hack-hunters-without-monsters","id":169939,"title":"Setting Hack- Hunters Without Monsters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-15T11:26:39-07:00","id":169939,"title":"Setting Hack- Hunters Without Monsters?","content":"Yep. Hunter without monsters.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that there are no supernatural beings/ phenomena/ items/ etc out there, just that there is no such thing as &quot;vampires&quot; or &quot;werewolves&quot;. There is a supernatural being who sucks blood, or something that changes between a man and a wolf, but those are unique phenomena, things that just happen- and they are rare, extremely rare. Most of the supernatural stuff is regular people who mess with weird stuff, which could be represented by supernatural merits.<br /> <br /> So, how would the Compacts/ Conspiracies would operate in such a world? After all, if regular people are the main users of all supernatural phenomena, and the conspiracies have tons of weird mojo in their disposal, would it make the Conspiracies in that hack into &quot;supernatural cuoporations&quot; which actually fight each other to control every piece of &quot;magic&quot; they can find? How would organizations which are focused around a specific type of beings, like the Cainte Heresy of the AKD, would adapt to this hack? Would certain Conpiracies just lose all of their meaning, while certain compacts would become even more important?<br /> <br /> it is just a thought exercise, so play along :P<br /> <br /> thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T14:36:55-07:00","id":170129,"title":"","content":"how they would operate is maybe the least interesting question you could draw from this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T15:39:21-07:00","id":170162,"title":"","content":"I supose it would mean stuff like Task Force Valkyrie and VASCU would become way more important, seeing as how they are the governments arm against all threats Supernal. They could direct alot of their efforts towards shutting down stuff like The Ashwood Abby, and the Lucifuge, which in the governments eyes would probably be a sadistic cult of killers, and abberant demon-spawn respectively. The Promethean Brotherhood and Aegis Kai Duro might just be seen as the antagonists of such a setting, as they would almost be the closest thing to real organised mages, in this setting. A few of Conspiracies would pretty much loose all meaning, though. Mostly the ones who deal specifically with 1 major type of supernatural. Like the ones who are Vampire Hunters, and the Mage Hunters from Witchfinders, come to mind.<br /> I almost sugest looking at an old Lovecraft story, actually. I think it was called &quot;The case of Charles Dexter Ward&quot;, in which a group of men become suspecious at the occult dealings of a man who lives in their town, and eventually invade his home to discover whatever horrors he has comitted. Setting idea kinda reminded me alittle of that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169939-setting-hack-hunters-without-monsters?p=170129#post170129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how they would operate is maybe the least interesting question you could draw from this</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Well, do you have any additional ideas for something more interesting? We'd all love to hear your ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T15:51:29-07:00","id":170167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169939-setting-hack-hunters-without-monsters#post169939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Hunter without monsters.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that there are no supernatural beings/ phenomena/ items/ etc out there, just that there is no such thing as &quot;vampires&quot; or &quot;werewolves&quot;. There is a supernatural being who sucks blood, or something that changes between a man and a wolf, but those are unique phenomena, things that just happen- and they are rare, extremely rare. Most of the supernatural stuff is regular people who mess with weird stuff, which could be represented by supernatural merits.<br /> <br /> So, how would the Compacts/ Conspiracies would operate in such a world? After all, if regular people are the main users of all supernatural phenomena, and the conspiracies have tons of weird mojo in their disposal, would it make the Conspiracies in that hack into &quot;supernatural cuoporations&quot; which actually fight each other to control every piece of &quot;magic&quot; they can find? How would organizations which are focused around a specific type of beings, like the Cainte Heresy of the AKD, would adapt to this hack? Would certain Conpiracies just lose all of their meaning, while certain compacts would become even more important?<br /> <br /> it is just a thought exercise, so play along :P<br /> <br /> thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know the Vigilante Militas down in mexico fighting off the cartels (while some of them become cartels unto themselves)? Run with that in a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T09:34:52-07:00","id":170820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169939-setting-hack-hunters-without-monsters?p=170129#post170129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how they would operate is maybe the least interesting question you could draw from this</div> </div> </div> </div>You are more than welcome to add your questions and how you would answer to them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Some thoughts about the core compacts/ conspiracies:<br /> <br /> Network- 0: I think that with the conspiracies holding most of the supernatural powers, they would focus most of their efforts on uncovering their secrets and true abilities to the wide population- which means that the conspiracies are going to really hate those guys :P<br /> <br /> The Union: instead of protection the population from the supernatural, they would protect the population in general, something like the Dollars from Durarara. They may even become a conspiracy, but that ain't really likely..<br /> <br /> Loyalists of Thule: with regular people being the major source of supernatural activity, and knowing that regular people mess up on daily basis, I can see those guys grow into a conspiracy quit quickly.<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey: so without monsters to hunt, they truly become an Hellfire Club, which messes with things it shouldn't do just for fun. Hunting a monster would be something really rare- and a great party- for them.<br /> <br /> Null Mysteriis- more or less the same<br /> <br /> Long Night: I assume that they would turn their efforts at either recruiting people/ collecting relics with certain supernatural powers (the gifts of God!) and destroy all others (spawn of satan!)<br /> <br /> Lucifuge: with no monsters to hunt, they'll have to find other ways to redeem their cursed blood- maybe by destroying wicked humans or something like that.<br /> <br /> Task Force: Valkyrie: without vampiric funding, they may find the money the need in the criminal underworld. Other than that, I believe they would stay the same, and just would focus their efforts against &quot;unauthorized magic users&quot;<br /> <br /> Aegis Kai Duro- why they lack their favorite prey, they still collect relics- and maybe they still believe themselves to once having so powerful magics they wish to reclaim.<br /> <br /> Ascending Ones- I think they would focus more of their efforts around the creation of Elixers and alchemy, with being used as diplomats between the different conspiracies while searching after the secrets of physical and spiritual perfection.<br /> <br /> Cheiron Group: so, if there aren't monsters to harvest, that is kinda a death blow for them, right? Unless they find a way to clone parts of the unique monsters that exist (which would make every monster taken as something which can not be replaced) or synthesis some weird organs out of pure magic, but they can't do that, right?... Right?...<br /> <br /> Malleus Maleficarum- without vampires, their founder seems to be dead and gone (unless he was effected by some weird magic which kept him alive). While they won't hunt vampires, they would be famous for calling down the powers of God when they are needed and will &quot;purify&quot; supernatural phenomena and the deeds of Satan.<br /> <br /> thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T06:52:12-07:00","id":172740,"title":"","content":"so- I'm bored again, so here are how I think the organizations from Witchfinders would look without witches to find :P<br /> <br /> Keepers of the Source- instead of protecting hallows from being used by witches, they would protect all kinds of supernatural phenomena: don't kill that creature! It is the last of its kind! Don't abuse the powers of relics! They are archeological wonders which should be preserved! Don't use supernatural energy! It harms the world's natural balance! Their Unseen Sense would become into a general thing, while they are going to be hated by the conspiracies just like Network-0, if not more<br /> <br /> Division VI- I think that in essence, they should still hunt from &quot;reality deviants&quot;, with such deviants being any person who use supernatural abilities. Of course, they should still be used by an higher organization, for it is a part of their theme, so I think it would be cool if they would not simply be used by some conspiracy to hunt its rivals, but by ALL of them. They switch superiors like one is changing socks, but all superiors claim to be a part of the same organization. One day, the hunt the Cainte Heresy, the next they hunt for the Cainte Heresy. This would make them into a wild card in the game the conspiracies play against each other.<br /> <br /> Promethean Brotherhood- so, because there are no witches to kill to steal their powers from, the firestealers should find another way to gain access to Mysteries- which is, by killing any person. Killing a monster would add +3 to the use of the Rite, while killing someone who is a normal mortal should be done with -2 penalty. Killing someone with supernatural abilities or destroying a relic would be counted as a &quot;witch&quot;.<br /> <br /> Knights of Saint George- They still serve the Faceless Angels and appease them by giving them magic so they could stay asleep. It is just that now, every type of supernatural power could be offered to the Angels, while on the outside they would claim that they protect the world from demons and the creations of hell. Actually, they may even become even more ritualistic, with killing someone/ destroying a phenomena who draws the attention of the sleeping gods must be done in a certain way, else the Angels won't get the sacrifice. They may even have to destroy a certain number of such phenomena in a certain time in order to stop their gods from awaken. The reason their powers are &quot;safe&quot; is because they use the dreams of the Angels ion order to invoke their Gospels, although it may be that the reason they destroy other supernatural phenomena is in order to be able to use their own powers without drawing the attention of the Angels. With the Knights, you can never tell when they lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T17:04:10-07:00","id":173349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/169939-setting-hack-hunters-without-monsters?p=172740#post172740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so- I'm bored again, so here are how I think the organizations from Witchfinders would look without witches to find :P<br /> <br /> Keepers of the Source- instead of protecting hallows from being used by witches, they would protect all kinds of supernatural phenomena: don't kill that creature! It is the last of its kind! Don't abuse the powers of relics! They are archeological wonders which should be preserved! Don't use supernatural energy! It harms the world's natural balance! Their Unseen Sense would become into a general thing, while they are going to be hated by the conspiracies just like Network-0, if not more<br /> <br /> Division VI- I think that in essence, they should still hunt from &quot;reality deviants&quot;, with such deviants being any person who use supernatural abilities. Of course, they should still be used by an higher organization, for it is a part of their theme, so I think it would be cool if they would not simply be used by some conspiracy to hunt its rivals, but by ALL of them. They switch superiors like one is changing socks, but all superiors claim to be a part of the same organization. One day, the hunt the Cainte Heresy, the next they hunt for the Cainte Heresy. This would make them into a wild card in the game the conspiracies play against each other.<br /> <br /> Promethean Brotherhood- so, because there are no witches to kill to steal their powers from, the firestealers should find another way to gain access to Mysteries- which is, by killing any person. Killing a monster would add +3 to the use of the Rite, while killing someone who is a normal mortal should be done with -2 penalty. Killing someone with supernatural abilities or destroying a relic would be counted as a &quot;witch&quot;.<br /> <br /> Knights of Saint George- They still serve the Faceless Angels and appease them by giving them magic so they could stay asleep. It is just that now, every type of supernatural power could be offered to the Angels, while on the outside they would claim that they protect the world from demons and the creations of hell. Actually, they may even become even more ritualistic, with killing someone/ destroying a phenomena who draws the attention of the sleeping gods must be done in a certain way, else the Angels won't get the sacrifice. They may even have to destroy a certain number of such phenomena in a certain time in order to stop their gods from awaken. The reason their powers are &quot;safe&quot; is because they use the dreams of the Angels ion order to invoke their Gospels, although it may be that the reason they destroy other supernatural phenomena is in order to be able to use their own powers without drawing the attention of the Angels. With the Knights, you can never tell when they lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>You kind of went the other way with the Keepers dog. The whole point of them was how the supernatural stuff was unnatural and harmful to the Earth on a fundamental level to the point where people 'attuned' to it would feel pain. I mean I don't see the logic in turning them into a PETA parody that wants to protect the supernatural just because of the hippie girl in the picture. It just doesn't make sense. Not every enivironmental activist is a pacifistic bleeding heart that only has the capacity to go around irritating the hard bitten badasses and reasonable people. <br /> <br /> People like to caricaturize the Keepers, but I think some of the ideas in that are pretty cool and they're underrated in a way. A lot of the groups outside the core are in my opinion. <br /> <br /> . I don't really get what you're trying to accomplish here. So like, what, no monsters? Conspiracies backstabbing each other, because they already got that. Division VI is a 'wild card', so what that means they're some directionless mess used to attack whatever's convenient?<br /> <br /> And you say there's no monsters, but what you really mean is no splats from the original post. The Promethean Brotherhood would be sort of hard to pull off if they're just going to sacrifice random stuff and hope it works. They were supposed to refine their methods over years. You can't do that if there's no consistency. Ain't nobody got time for that. Can't really do much with the Knights or the Promethean Brotherhood without some more thought into what you're rewriting because of their ties to witches and stuff. I don't think there was ever anything about the Knights doing sacrifices and it just doesn't seem right for an organization that's supposed to be easing people into the idea of Faceless angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3309-electrick","name":"electrick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}